    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The three test files are the only ones: `AcceptanceTest` (the one runnable test), plus the abstract base and the audit-capture utility. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping sequence numbers, and propagated that identity to everything derived from it.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 rewrote `generateCustomerCode(owner)`:\n- `REGION` = `owner.getRegion()` (region derived from the postcode, with the existing city fallback)\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (the telephone is already normalized to E.164 by the time this runs)\n- removed the now-unused `firstThreeLetters` helper and the per-city sequence lookup from code generation (`countOwnersInCity` is retained \u2014 it still backs the per-city capacity cap)\n\nThe **membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its **Luhn check digit** (`Owner.getCheckDigit()` over the code's digits), and the **create audit record** (`AUDIT.info(\"... customerCode={} ...\")`) all derive from `customerCode`, so they automatically move to the new identity \u2014 confirmed by the audit line `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 `getLocality()` now derives from the region-and-hash `customerCode` (the segment before the first `-`), falling back to `getRegion()` when no code is assigned yet. The value is identical to the old region-based result but is now literally sourced from the new identity.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples to match the new format.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` (asserts `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) and the whole suite pass.",
